# Power button (2026-11-18, user's request): the keyboard's T16 - top row, last column, the orange power keycap.
# The keyboard microcontroller reads that optical key (also while the board is off: the keyboard is fed from
# VCC5V_BUS) and pulls PMIC_PWRON low over the keyboard harness J20 pin 5 (34_hub_link.net), the way a PC's
# front-panel button reaches its motherboard.  The RK817's power-key logic is unchanged: a press switches the board
# on; while it runs a short press is a power-key event for the OS, about 6 s held cuts the power.
# (A panel-mount button in the codec cover was looked at first: no 12-19 mm one fits - 12 mm of room under the cover.)
SHEET pmic
# the line leaves the board: ESD at the connector
ED13 ESD:BTR04G02 PMIC_PWRON GND
# service fallback, not fitted: the old side-operated tact switch on the column's left edge, in case the keyboard's
# firmware is not there (bring-up) or hangs
SW3 TACT_SIDE:DNP 1=PMIC_PWRON 2=GND
